{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1529059-ballard-family-as-a-giovanni-minor-clan","id":1529059,"title":"Ballard family as a Giovanni minor clan","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-01-20T19:02:29-08:00","id":1529059,"title":"Ballard family as a Giovanni minor clan","content":"V5 Chicago gave us a brief plot hook where the Boston Giovanni approach Horatio Ballard with an offer to have his mortal kin become a minor family in the Hecata. My Midwest focused game is overly infested with the Giovanni families so I kinda wanted to pursue this idea, but I struggled to think of a way to make the Ballards unique from the other money-making Giovanni associate families like the Milliners and Dunsirn. Horatio Ballard has a knack for sniffing out opportunities since he learned about vampires after a few heart attacks and even managed to find Lodin, plus V5 CbN has him embracing technology by testing a few &quot;SchrekNET-lite&quot; projects which he doesn't really understand the danger of when the SI inevitably crack into them.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I interpreted this as the Ballard family becoming more adventurous and experimental with their investments and schemes, being the technological Steve Jobs-esque family who relies on Horatio's status and (quickly depleting) wealth to test the financial waters to tap into markets which are rapidly expanding in the modern age (general tech, AI, weed dispensaries, OnlyFans, maybe dropping their own crypto-currency when they saw how BitCoin took off). Their Disciplines could be either Dominate, Presence and Necromancy (Oblivion) to embrace the Ventrue's overwhelming leadership ideal, or maybe Fortitude, Presence and Necroblivion since they're used to kowtowing to Horatio and embrace the soft-power kind of mindset. Maybe not even bothering with Necromancy to go with Auspex, Fortitude and Presence/Dominate? Auspex would fit a minor family on the lookout for the right opportunities<br /> <br /> Would you have the Hecata extend the offer to the Ballards in your game? If so, should Horatio jump ship and not even wait to see what happens when the Promise of 1528 expires just to reap the benefits affiliating with the Hecata could give him considering how he's not exactly thriving at the moment? What Discipline set would you give them?<br /> <br /> A little off-topic but has anyone created their own Giovanni minor family, maybe went political with the Kennedy's to really mess with the Milliners? Let this be a general minor family discussion thread if you will. Thanks for reading if you did : )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28284,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28284-abugintherug","user":"abugintherug","date":". 01-20-2024, 11:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28284-abugintherug","name":"abugintherug","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28284_2.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-22T05:22:41-08:00","id":1529147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>abugintherug</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1529059-ballard-family-as-a-giovanni-minor-clan#post1529059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I struggled to think of a way to make the Ballards unique from the other money-making Giovanni associate families</div> </div> </div> </div>If we consider Horatio Ballard was born in 1832 as a son of an Albany businessman and legislator (Albany has been a center for banking, railroads, and international trade) and when America's industrial barons, like the Rockefellers and Vanderbilts bloomed as they tried to milk the government for money while the nation was being rebuilt, none of Chicago's financial cutthroats could compare to Ballard in pure ruthlessness and guile and Ballard's uncle already owned Chicago's largest construction companies when he died and Horatio inherited his business, I would say we have a nice setup<br /> More so, his sheet says: Finance (Industry) 4 - and his touchstone mentins the Ballard Industries<br /> So I would say the Ballards were/are focused on that deparment and area<br /> In the modern era, especially such turbulent times, construction and industry are bread and butter - rebuild war torn areas for Kindred and Kin alike.. not to mention with a rempaging Second Inquisition around, building very secure havens for Vampires with top-notch securtiy systems (for money and boons)<br /> Dominate, Presence and Fortitude sounds right for the family (especially if you want to breed them as Ravenants - not unheard of, take the Servants of Anushin-Rawan for example, Ventrue Ravenants - Horatio's Disciplines were Dominate, Fortitude, Presence with a tiny Potance)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 01-22-2024, 09:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-22T07:18:17-08:00","id":1529150,"title":"","content":"I really like this discussion and I agree that the Ballards would work great as a Hecata minor family.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-22T08:05:09-08:00","id":1529153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1529059-ballard-family-as-a-giovanni-minor-clan?p=1529147#post1529147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> rebuild war torn areas for Kindred and Kin alike..</div> </div> </div> </div>I dig this angle, its really useful and absolutely necessary. Using Ballard Industries as a legitimate front to better develop parts of the city for Camarilla control and leaving the Anarch territory struggling like he did to Gary, Indiana. I suppose that would mean the family embracing the corporate role? I think only the Koenigs with their arms industry would have a similar family culture, if the Ballards specialize in construction contracts and launder cash, give no-show jobs to further add to someone's Mask/mortal identity, buy up more of the white-collar businesses in the city, I think thats definitely a unique niche they could fill. Don't mind if I run with this<br /> <br /> As for Disciplines thats up to personal taste for how we'd all use them in our games, I'm definitely set on the Ballards having Dominate like most Giovanni and throwing in Presence for a little taste of Ventrue. But I'm tempted to swap Fortitude for Potence instead, especially since you mentioned Horatio dabbles with it. If the family who would eventually be the first Ballard minor clan vampires have been ghouled beforehand they'd definitely have some experience with Potence, plus Fortitude in v5 makes people harder to Dominate which I doubt Horatio would want to deal with. So Dominate and Potence like most Gio's have, then Presence for the subtle manipulation the Ventrue go for? This part I'm still undecided about<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28284-abugintherug","name":"abugintherug","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28284_2.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-22T12:00:40-08:00","id":1529162,"title":"","content":"It would make for a great future Ventrue and Hecate tensions as Mr. Ballard is Ventrue but encourages his family to join up with the Hecate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-22T19:33:31-08:00","id":1529191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1529059-ballard-family-as-a-giovanni-minor-clan?p=1529162#post1529162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would make for a great future Ventrue and Hecate tensions as Mr. Ballard is Ventrue but encourages his family to join up with the Hecate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, nothing to stop him of participating on some weird blood rituals in the vein (oops) of Baali's <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Baali?so=search#Apostates\" target=\"_blank\">Rite of Apostasy</a>, if some group in contemporary has chances of possessing such a thing is a melange of Cappadocian remnant bloodlines (and Nagaraja gone rogue from the Tal'Mahe'Ra) being led by Lazarus of all people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-22T23:29:42-08:00","id":1529208,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Lucida Sans Unicode\">That would mean the Final Death of Horatio Ballard because as more members of their family become vampires from the Hecata/Giovanni clan and gain access to his family fortune they are just gonna rebel against him in a very hostile take over.<br /> <br /> Ballard best resource are his family assets and his herd which is his family, he cannot give them without losing his power.<br /> <br /> Also the Ventrue aren\u00b4t going to leave someone as influential despite his age like Ballard get taken over that easily because many have invested in him. Getting their assets stolen does not make elders happy.</span><br /> <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Lucida Sans Unicode\">Personally I would hate this because Ballard as a character was built since 1st EDITION to be someone that <b><u>the players have to choose</u></b> between destroying or not, because doing so would cause an economic recession and create a lot of enemies who got their assets frozen after Ballard Death.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16","name":"Leandro16","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24037_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-23T09:32:08-08:00","id":1529224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leandro16</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1529059-ballard-family-as-a-giovanni-minor-clan?p=1529208#post1529208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That would mean the Final Death of Horatio Ballard because as more members of their family become vampires from the Hecata/Giovanni clan and gain access to his family fortune they are just gonna rebel against him in a very hostile take over.<br /> <br /> Ballard best resource are his family assets and his herd which is his family, he cannot give them without losing his power.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering how he's victimized his family for decades upon decades thats probably going to happen eventually, so you aren't wrong. The question is if Ballard is desperate for success enough to risk giving his herd a longer leash and let someone else hold onto it. You could definitely say he wouldn't risk it, but I'm inclined to go for it<br /> <br /> The benefits to the whole deal aren't going to be found elsewhere and the dangers are something he can both predict and prepare for. The young Giovanni had the assistance of elder Cappadocians/Harbingers and who knows how many bloodlines to overthrow their dominators, who do the mortal Ballards have? Capone and the Anarchs? Any Giovanni old and powerful enough to be his rivals probably became supper back at the Family Reunion. Just have him Embrace the cream of the crop among the family as his own and now they too have good reason to keep the Ventrue as majority shareholders<br /> <br /> But I don't see the other Ventrue taking offense to it if he did go through with it. He himself is still Ventrue and he'd be retaining control over his regrowing assets, its a risky investment which are always the best for someone else to pursue. They never had control over the Ballard family themselves so they're gambling with someone else's chips. So long as he's paying his dues what reason do they have to criticize him?<br /> <br /> A chance to build ties with the Hecata and ease tensions with the Cappadocians in that sect/clan is well worth the risk imo, the Ventrue probably never expected to cross a bridge they burned 500 years ago. Maybe a few Cappies will be willing to mirror his move and dip a toe back into the Camarilla. Kevin Jackson's the unexpected diplomat with the Lasombra, Horatio can be the ambassador to the former allies they'd thrown to the wolves<br /> <br /> And if it all did go belly up and Ballard loses everything? It'd sting, but he's not exactly well-liked and irreplaceable. Would take years to recover the influence he had over the mortal sector but there's always a hungry neonate looking to prove themself, Lodin's brood have always had a stranglehold on Chicago. Capone would probably slide in, lament not being to one to &quot;ash that bloated walrus&quot;, then gobble up most of the businesses lost in the fray.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28284-abugintherug","name":"abugintherug","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28284_2.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-23T13:27:08-08:00","id":1529240,"title":"","content":"Yes I could see some of the younger members of the Ballard family doing away with Horatio as they got a stronger taste of power and freedom.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-23T15:27:56-08:00","id":1529257,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28284-abugintherug\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar28284_2.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"28284\" data-vbnamecard=\"28284\">abugintherug</a> <br /> <br /> Interesting fact,<br /> <br /> One of the things I noticed they changed for Chicago V5 is that Horatio Ballard's &quot;Creepy Uncle&quot; qualities have been removed. I think they wanted to get away from the Edgelord elements of the original Chicago by Night as much as possible. This is why Jacob Schumpeter is killed off by the Second Inquisition (though I believe that may have simply been a preference by Matthew Dawkins, to which I say, *fist bump*).<br /> <br /> The new version of Horatio Ballard is much more focused on being a Ventrue who has lost his ungodly amounts of wealth and is trying to rebuild it. Which, honestly, since he's got Dominate and Finance 5 shouldn't be that difficult. Financial crime is something I doubt that vampires have difficulty with.<br /> <br /> Though if I were doing Ballard in &quot;our&quot; world, I'd reveal that he was completely taken in by Madoff and tried to fix the problem with real estate and ended up getting hit by 2008's Financial Collapse. Which, in other words, means he's lost not millions of dollars but BILLIONS. Maybe enough that if it was ever found out by the rest of Clan Ventrue, he'd be the laughing stock of the clan or staked because a lot of that was the Clan's money.<br /> <br /> My take on the subject of Ballard joining Clan Giovanni is that it is a desperation ploy because Horatio Ballard has to suspect that joining the Giovanni Clan is something that he, as a Ventrue, has no place in. The thing is that Clan Giovanni is kind of on the outs and the other Clans are on the rise, which means that whatever plans they HAD for the Ballard clan (small c) is probably gone but individual families like the Pisanob might be willing to ally with them anyway.<br /> <br /> There could be &quot;leverage&quot; from the Ballards, especially if Horatio offers to set the Hecata up in Chicago or some other element of the family. The Hecata has money to burn after all and Ballard has a serious cash flow problem.<br /> <br /> But that doesn't mean the Hecata want to SHARE with a disgraced Ventrue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-23T17:40:48-08:00","id":1529264,"title":"","content":"It certainly is an offer thats too good to be true and would be the final nail in Ballard's coffin, but the only way I could see that going down is if someone from the family (probably a PC) is the one to rise up and take his place. The Gio's aren't in a great bargaining position so he'd be wary of them and put plenty of thought into the negotiations, its his herd on the bargaining table after all. But he'd underestimate the mortal Ballards who've been under his thumb for so long, though he'd still take measures to prevent them from doing what the Hecata did to the Anziani and Augustus<br /> <br /> Maybe one of them has an elder Mawla who teaches them Necromancy? All the money in the world can't save you from ghosts. Or maybe one just has the willpower to break through the mental conditioning in a vulnerable moment and does something drastic like diablerizes him<br /> <br /> He's a bit of a roach who likely died in countless chronicles two decades ago but survives in the canon plot despite everything, I have to give him some credit. A Ballard minor family is more interesting if he's out of the picture, it just has to be more compelling than &quot;the Giovanni outnumber him and push him out of the company and his Ventrue allies don't bother to save him afterward.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28284-abugintherug","name":"abugintherug","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28284_2.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-23T19:21:14-08:00","id":1529266,"title":"","content":"I think if people like Ballard as a villain depends if you see him as more like Jabba the Hutt or Wilson Fisk.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-23T22:02:14-08:00","id":1529281,"title":"","content":"I always saw Ballard as someone like Sydney Greenstart in the Maltese Falcon.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GpMj0dnYg8Y\" data-code=\"GpMj0dnYg8Y\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/GpMj0dnYg8Y/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> Horatio Ballard is a Ventrue. He could never be a member of the Hecata/Giovanni. All the various bloodlines that became the Hecata were in fact descendants of Cappadocius and thus one clan except for the Nagaraja whose inclusion was always bullshit. So to be honest, I think the premise of the OP to be ridiculous. You can't change your clan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-24T07:46:50-08:00","id":1529306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-worl